content:
The age breakdown does not yield an independent equation for \(T\); using the gender totals:

\[
120=0.60\cdot \frac{T}{3}+0.40\cdot \frac{2T}{3}
=\frac{7T}{15}
\]

So

\[
T=\frac{1800}{7}
\]

Thus the number of women is

\[
T-120=\frac{1800}{7}-120=\frac{960}{7}
\]

\[
\boxed{\frac{960}{7}}
\]
